        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "576c53a8-9b26-3ba7-9e5c-8b73ecf19782",
                "word": "sous-culture",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1c4bd5b1-07f6-4350-87bc-241e9e57fc58",
                        "entry_id": "576c53a8-9b26-3ba7-9e5c-8b73ecf19782",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sous-cultures"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bdb86cdb-7675-31c3-8006-7a637d77f5bd",
                        "entry_id": "576c53a8-9b26-3ba7-9e5c-8b73ecf19782",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Culture d’un sous-groupe de la société globale présentant des variantes par rapport à la culture dominante."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ff8663c-de95-4119-9d62-fb1862273a48",
                                "sense_id": "bdb86cdb-7675-31c3-8006-7a637d77f5bd",
                                "text": "Bien évidemment, une culture peut se subdiviser en un certain nombre de sous-cultures, correspondant à des différenciations objectives de l'environnement, ou des conditions de vie (sous-culture rurale et sous-culture urbaine, par exemple), mais ces sous-cultures partagent la plus grande partie des unités de sens qui forment la culture globale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a7d485a-3dae-46e2-8c4e-83165c7c3f03",
                                "sense_id": "bdb86cdb-7675-31c3-8006-7a637d77f5bd",
                                "text": "La notion de sous-culture est relative. En effet, chaque culture peut être une sous-culture si on l’étudie dans sa relation avec une culture plus large : la culture belge ou la culture française sont des sous-cultures par rapport notamment à la culture européenne."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d32c913f-e3a2-32fc-bb34-590e36a15e17",
                        "entry_id": "576c53a8-9b26-3ba7-9e5c-8b73ecf19782",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Culture considérée comme de moindre valeur qu’une autre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cb36682-529d-411e-a021-3e33dce7438e",
                                "sense_id": "d32c913f-e3a2-32fc-bb34-590e36a15e17",
                                "text": "Et c’est à l’heure où, dans l’avant-dernier virage, la culture de gauche, avec ses opérations Disneyland, la cinquième chaîne, sombrait dans la sous-culture plouc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "daf1db9c-2b98-4013-89bf-e494f29ace2c",
                                "sense_id": "d32c913f-e3a2-32fc-bb34-590e36a15e17",
                                "text": "Dans sa jeunesse, le Californien hirsute, pour échapper au quotidien monotone de Burbank, la banlieue pavillonnaire de Los Angeles où il a grandi, s’est construit un imaginaire très personnel nourri de romantisme gothique, d’expressionnisme européen et de sous-culture américaine. Dans sa tête se bousculent Frankenstein, Edgar Allan Poe, Ed Wood, Nosferatu, la revue « MAD », les films de la Hammer, les créatures de Ray Harryhausen, l’imagerie foraine, celle des fêtes populaires…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eed90ed9-4f5e-46d1-9ce1-964ae990d4be",
                                "sense_id": "d32c913f-e3a2-32fc-bb34-590e36a15e17",
                                "text": "Violences qui s’inscrivent, enfin, dans un contexte culturo-médiatique maintes fois dénoncé, ce que les observateurs nomment volontiers « la sous-culture des feuilletons et films américains »."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84f70c6e-c22d-4d0c-9fe5-3cfce10a4ab4",
                        "source_entry_id": "576c53a8-9b26-3ba7-9e5c-8b73ecf19782",
                        "source_sense_description": "sociologie",
                        "target_lang_word": "subculture",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "subculture",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f893a939-8117-3946-ac02-a581dd0ba138",
                                        "entry_id": "724ac046-07cb-3525-a4f9-20c6b23ad15c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A portion of a culture distinguished by its customs or other features, often in contrast to the larger mainstream culture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ad34ec0-bba7-4763-b04f-efba7d26d115",
                                                "sense_id": "f893a939-8117-3946-ac02-a581dd0ba138",
                                                "text": "The goth subculture has its own mode of dress, and it has a characteristic musical style."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b70d3ec-e8e8-437e-b5e3-2370fecfe9ef",
                                                "sense_id": "f893a939-8117-3946-ac02-a581dd0ba138",
                                                "text": "Like those activities, bodybuilding is an obsession, a living (for a few), and a way of life for the people involved in it—a subculture, in a word, with its own values, aesthetics and vocabulary."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "761fb294-374b-4ecf-919d-d737deaf4603",
                                                "sense_id": "f893a939-8117-3946-ac02-a581dd0ba138",
                                                "text": "Joybubbles (the legal name of the former Joe Engressia since 1991), a blind genius with perfect pitch who accidentally found he could make free phone calls by whistling tones and went on to play a pivotal role in the 1970s subculture of “phone phreaks,” died on Aug. 8 in Minneapolis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00b8568c-a8d7-4db8-979d-1ddafb9bde09",
                                                "sense_id": "f893a939-8117-3946-ac02-a581dd0ba138",
                                                "text": "White Americans are transitioning toward minority status for the first time. As they do, perhaps their ways will be treated less as the default mainstream, and more as subcultures among subcultures."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bafa9997-ed69-4c08-bbc6-5b92da6e1eab",
                                                "sense_id": "f893a939-8117-3946-ac02-a581dd0ba138",
                                                "text": "White evangelicals once saw themselves “as the owners of mainstream American culture and morality and values,” said Jones. Now they are just another subculture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e06e24a-93be-3022-87b5-af3a9bd9bc8c",
                                        "entry_id": "724ac046-07cb-3525-a4f9-20c6b23ad15c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A culture made by transferring microorganisms from a previous culture to a fresh growth medium"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "subculture",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "180d0daa-8d72-3c9f-bdc5-5ef4b57e0d17",
                                        "entry_id": "dafb029b-4d18-3ad3-8b01-662527cd5571",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To transfer (microorganisms) to a fresh growth medium in order to start a new culture"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d2bdffd-97a3-4aad-90df-159ead0514cb",
                                                "sense_id": "180d0daa-8d72-3c9f-bdc5-5ef4b57e0d17",
                                                "text": "Cultures were subcultured by 20-fold dilution into fresh MS2D medium approximately every 7 d."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
